
==========================================================================================================
  D1  mu_dS IN CLOSED FORM, AND ITS TWO LIMITS
==========================================================================================================
  mu_dS(a) = [sqrt(a^2 + a_dS^2) - a_dS]/a = (-a_dS + sqrt(a**2 + a_dS**2))/a
  in u = a/a_dS:   mu_dS(u) = (sqrt(u**2 + 1) - 1)/u
  u -> infinity:  mu_dS -> 1      (Newtonian)
  u -> 0:         mu_dS -> u/2      (deep MOND)
  [OK] D1a mu_dS -> 1 at large acceleration and -> u/2 at small, so it interpolates correctly and its deep-regime slope is 1/2 in u. The 1/2 is what fixes the coefficient in D3 -- it is not free
  [OK] D1b and mu_dS contains NO 2 pi and NO hbar: both sit in the common prefactor of T(a) and cancel in the ratio. *** That is precisely why the correct de Sitter-Unruh coefficient carries no 2 pi, and why my frequency-based reading in the previous swing was wrong. ***

==========================================================================================================
  D2  IS IT THE FRAMEWORK'S alpha=1 KERNEL? -- symbolic identity test
==========================================================================================================
  framework alpha=1:  from g_obs^2 = g_bar^2 + g_bar a0,   mu_1(x) = (sqrt(4*x**2 + 1) - 1)/(2*x)   (x = g_obs/a0)
  mu_dS with the mechanism's own a0 = 2 a_dS (so u = 2x):   mu_dS = (sqrt(4*x**2 + 1) - 1)/(2*x)
  [OK] D2a *** THEY ARE THE SAME FUNCTION. Residual = 0, identically. *** The de Sitter-Unruh interpolation IS the framework's alpha=1 kernel, exactly, with no adjustment. So the framework's kernel shape is NOT an arbitrary choice -- it is what the mechanism produces. That is a genuine vindication of the kernel, and it is prior art (Milgrom 1999; the construction appears in his own pedagogical review)
  [OK] D2b cross-check in the corpus's own published form: mu_1 reproduces g_obs^2 = g_bar^2 + g_bar a0 identically, so D2a is a statement about the framework's PUBLISHED law and not about a paraphrase

==========================================================================================================
  D3  THE COEFFICIENT THE SAME DERIVATION FORCES
==========================================================================================================
  the mechanism forces a0 = 2 a_dS = 2 c H_Lambda, i.e. Z = 1/2, kappa = 4*sqrt(6)*sqrt(pi)/3 = 5.78881
  the framework uses kappa = 1/2, i.e. Z = 2 sqrt(8pi/3) = 4*sqrt(6)*sqrt(pi)/3 = 5.78881
  ratio = 8*sqrt(6)*sqrt(pi)/3 = 11.5776
  [OK] D3a *** THE PACKAGE IS INSEPARABLE AND THE FRAMEWORK TAKES HALF OF IT. *** The same one-line construction that gives the framework its kernel (D2a) also forces a0 = 2 c H_Lambda, which is 11.58x = 4 sqrt(8pi/3) times the framework's value. Written the clean way: the framework's Z = 2 sqrt(8pi/3) EXACTLY (identical to sqrt(32pi/3)), so its coefficient is one factor of 2 in Z away from the kappa = 1 reference sqrt(8pi/3), and the mechanism's output sits 4 sqrt(8pi/3) away from it. The framework adopts the kernel and rejects the coefficient by that factor. This is not new to the corpus -- A0_HALF_THE_DARK_ENERGY_RATE already states the 11.58x -- but the KERNEL half of the package is not stated anywhere, and it is what makes the rejection costly rather than free

==========================================================================================================
  D4  WHAT THE alpha=1 -> alpha=2 SWITCH COSTS, UNPRICED UNTIL NOW
==========================================================================================================
  the kernel now in force (alpha=2):  mu_2(x) = x/sqrt(x**2 + 1)
  mu_2(1) = sqrt(2)/2 = 0.707107 against mu_1(1) = 0.618034
  [OK] D4a *** THE alpha=2 KERNEL IS NOT THE de SITTER-UNRUH KERNEL. *** mu_2 != mu_dS as functions (they differ by 0.0891 at x = 1, 14.4%). So the alpha=1 -> alpha=2 switch -- made for solar-system reasons -- ALSO costs the framework the mechanism's derivation of its kernel shape. The corpus priced that switch at +0.0033 dex on SPARC plus ephemeris relief; it did NOT price the loss of the de Sitter-Unruh derivation of the kernel, and that is a real cost this script is the first to state

  THE HONEST LEDGER ON THE SWITCH, both directions:
   * alpha=1 KEEPS the de Sitter-Unruh derivation of the kernel (D2a) but carries the Sun-binding ephemeris
     liability at 1279x the Earth bound, post-EFE = bare (mi_efe_escape_and_ch23_withdrawn_2026).
   * alpha=2 fixes the ephemeris to 6.2-12.4x (still failing, mi_alpha2_sun_reflex_2026) but FORFEITS the
     kernel derivation.
  Neither kernel is free. That trade is now explicit and was not before.

==========================================================================================================
  D5  THE WITHDRAWAL, QUANTIFIED
==========================================================================================================
  my previous claim (frequency identification):  Z = 2*pi -> a0 = c H_Lambda/2pi
  the correct acceleration identification:       Z = 1/2 -> a0 = 2 c H_Lambda
  they disagree by a factor 4*pi = 12.566
  [OK] D5a *** MY cH_Lambda/2pi 'DERIVATION' IS WITHDRAWN. *** It disagrees with the standard construction by exactly 4*pi = 4 pi = 12.57 (I first wrote 4 pi^2 -- corrected), and the standard construction is the correct one: the 2 pi and the hbar cancel out of mu (D1b), so a turnover condition on the ACCELERATION carries no 2 pi. My reading identified the kernel's FREQUENCY unit with the thermal frequency k_B T/hbar, which is an extra, unforced conversion. The claim that the de Sitter tie 'derives kappa = sqrt(2/(3pi))' must not be repeated

  WHAT SURVIVES FROM THAT SWING, unchanged: the two no-go results, which are arithmetic about Z and are
  independent of which identification is used --
   * Z^2/pi = 32/3 is rational while Z/pi^k is irrational for every integer k, so rational x pi^k ingredients
     can force Z^2 but never Z;
   * quadratic-in-Z, hbar-free, and carrying the Bekenstein-Hawking 1/4 are jointly unsatisfiable.
  And what survives is now sharper, because the de Sitter mechanism's actual output is a RATIONAL multiple of
  cH_Lambda (namely 2), which is in the barred class for Z = sqrt(32pi/3) exactly as those theorems predict.

  *** NET EFFECT ON THE FRAMEWORK, stated both ways. *** BETTER: its alpha=1 kernel is derived, not chosen --
  the de Sitter-Unruh mechanism produces it exactly (D2a), which is a substantive result the corpus did not
  have. WORSE: the same derivation forces a0 = 2 c H_Lambda, 11.58x the framework's value (D3a), and the
  alpha=2 switch now in force forfeits the kernel derivation entirely (D4a). The framework cannot hold the
  kernel derivation and the coefficient at the same time, and under alpha=2 it holds neither.

